  "nl_text": "The database schema rschema_0248 is used to store information about users, articles, books, activities, video interviews, user comments, book recommendations, activity lotteries, and user activity participation. The schema consists of nine tables: User, Article, Book, Activity, Video_Interview, User_Comments, Book_Recommendation, Activity_Lottery, and User_Activity_Participation.\nThe User table contains information about users, including their last login time, password, registration time, role, user ID, and username. The Article table contains information about articles, including article ID, author, content, publish time, and title. The Book table contains information about books, including author, book description, book ID, and title. The Activity table contains information about activities, including activity ID, activity description, activity name, and activity time. The Video_Interview table contains information about video interviews, including publish time, title, video ID, and video link.\nThe User_Comments table contains information about user comments on articles, including article ID, comment content, comment time, and user ID. The Book_Recommendation table contains information about book recommendations, including book ID, book review, recommendation reason, recommendation time, and recommender ID. The Activity_Lottery table contains information about activity lotteries, including activity ID, prize name, winner ID, and participation time. The User_Activity_Participation table contains information about user participation in activities, including activity ID, participation time, and user ID.\nEach table has its own primary key, and some tables have foreign keys that reference other tables. For example, the User_Comments table has foreign keys that reference the Article and User tables, while the Book_Recommendation table has foreign keys that reference the Book and User tables. The foreign keys ensure that the data in the tables is consistent and accurate, and that the relationships between the tables are properly maintained.\nOverall, the schema is designed to store and manage information about users, articles, books, activities, video interviews, user comments, book recommendations, activity lotteries, and user activity participation. It provides a comprehensive and consistent way to store and retrieve data, and ensures that the data is accurate and consistent across the different tables.",
  "gold_question": "The system is a user-article sharing forum with the following features:\n1.User Interaction Features:\nEach user has a unique User ID, Username, Password, Registration Time, Last Login Time, and Role.\nA user can participate in multiple activities, engage in video interviews, and comment or recommend books and articles.\n2.Content Management:\nThe system manages several books and articles.\nBook Information: Each book has a Book ID, Title, Author, and Description.\nArticle Information: Each article has an Article ID, Title, Content, Author, and Publish Time.\nActivity Information: Each activity has an Activity ID, Activity Name, Activity Time, and Description.\nVideo Interview Information: Each video interview has a Video ID, Title, Video Link, and Publish Time.\n3.Activity Management:\nThe system can organize source code reading activities, record activity names, times, and descriptions.\nUsers can participate in multiple activities.\nThe system also handles lottery activities, recording winner information and awarding gifts.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0248.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0248\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_login_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `article` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `author` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `publish_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `book_description` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `activity` (\n  `activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `activity_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_description` text NOT NULL,\n  `activity_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`activity_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `video_interview` (\n  `video_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `video_link` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `publish_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`video_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_comments` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `comment_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `comment_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_recommendation` (\n  `recommendation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `recommender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `recommendation_reason` text NOT NULL,\n  `book_review` text NOT NULL,\n  `recommendation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`recommendation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_recommendation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_recommendation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`recommender_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `activity_lottery` (\n  `lottery_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `winner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `prize_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `participation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`lottery_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `activity_lottery_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`activity_id`) REFERENCES `activity` (`activity_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `activity_lottery_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`winner_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_activity_participation` (\n  `participation_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `participation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`participation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_activity_participation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_activity_participation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`activity_id`) REFERENCES `activity` (`activity_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
